---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HTTP API contracts — .NET Challenges"
  description="Practice the validation and problem-response decision for HTTP API writes."
>
  <main id="main" class="challenge">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href={base}>All available challenges</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">HTTP API contracts</span>
    </nav>

    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Sequence 01 <span>/ 09</span> · API ACTION</p>
        <h1 id="challenge-title">HTTP API contracts</h1>
        <p class="hero-summary">
          Make an invalid write a clear response, not a change hidden in the store.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="status-slip" aria-label="Example invalid request and its required effect">
        <div class="slip-top">
          <span>Request trace</span>
          <span>01 / 04</span>
        </div>
        <code class="slip-route">POST /products</code>
        <pre><code>{`{ "name": " ", "quantity": 0 }`}</code></pre>
        <p class="slip-result">
          <span class="stamp">400</span>
          <span>problem names both fields</span>
        </p>
        <p class="slip-result">
          <span class="state-mark" aria-hidden="true">=</span>
          <span>stored product stays unchanged</span>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <div class="content-grid">
      <div class="main-column">
        <section class="content-section decision" aria-labelledby="decision-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">The decision</p>
          <h2 id="decision-title">
            A create or replace whose <code>name</code> has no non-whitespace character, or
            whose <code>quantity</code> is outside 1 to 100, returns 400 with a problem
            response that names each invalid member, and the stored product is unchanged.
          </h2>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section effects" aria-labelledby="effects-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="section-kicker">What a local pass proves</p>
              <h2 id="effects-title">Required effects</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="effect-count">4 checks</span>
          </div>
          <p class="effect-contract">
            Each test starts from an empty product store. No test reads or writes another
            test's products. A local pass does not depend on test order. A 400 effect is
            status 400, media type <code>application/problem+json</code>, and an
            <code>errors</code> entry for every invalid member, matched without regard to
            case. Message text, <code>type</code>, <code>title</code>, and
            <code>traceId</code> stay outside the effect.
          </p>
          <ol class="effect-list">
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">01</span>
              <p>
                <code>POST /products</code> with <code>{`{ "name": " ", "quantity": 0 }`}</code>
                returns that 400, with <code>errors</code> entries for <code>name</code> and
                <code>quantity</code>. <code>GET /products</code> returns an empty collection.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">02</span>
              <p>
                <code>POST /products</code> with <code>{`{ "name": "", "quantity": 101 }`}</code>
                returns that same 400. <code>GET /products</code> returns an empty collection.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">03</span>
              <p>
                <code>POST /products</code> with <code>{`{ "name": "a", "quantity": 1 }`}</code>
                returns 201. <code>GET /products</code> returns one product with that name and
                quantity. <code>PUT /products/{`{id}`}</code> with
                <code>{`{ "name": " ", "quantity": 0 }`}</code> returns that 400, and
                <code>GET /products/{`{id}`}</code> still returns name <code>a</code> and
                quantity 1. <code>PUT /products/{`{id}`}</code> with
                <code>{`{ "name": "a", "quantity": 100 }`}</code> returns 204, and
                <code>GET /products/{`{id}`}</code> returns name <code>a</code> and quantity 100.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="effect-number">04</span>
              <p>
                <code>GET /products/{`{id}`}</code> for an id that is not stored returns 404.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="effect-boundary">
            A replace of a product that is not stored is outside the effects, whether or not
            the body breaks the rules. The harness replaces only a product that is already
            stored.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section guidance" aria-labelledby="hints-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">Ask for a nudge</p>
          <h2 id="hints-title">Hints</h2>
          <div class="disclosures">
            <details data-reveal="http-hint-1" data-hint-number="1">
              <summary><span>Hint 1</span><span class="summary-label">Name the behavior</span></summary>
              <p>
                A create or replace whose name has no non-whitespace character, or whose
                quantity is outside 1 to 100, must return a problem response that names
                each invalid member and must leave the stored product unchanged. A 400
                whose body is a plain message still fails.
              </p>
            </details>
            <div data-hint-gate="2" hidden>
              <details data-reveal="http-hint-2" data-hint-number="2">
                <summary><span>Hint 2</span><span class="summary-label">Find the framework area</span></summary>
                <p>Model validation and validation problem details.</p>
              </details>
            </div>
            <div data-hint-gate="3" hidden>
              <details data-reveal="http-hint-3" data-hint-number="3">
                <summary><span>Hint 3</span><span class="summary-label">Narrow the approach</span></summary>
                <p>
                  Validate the body before it is saved, on both writes, and return a
                  validation problem that names the invalid members. A required-string
                  check still accepts a name made only of spaces, so that create returns
                  201 and stores the product.
                </p>
              </details>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="content-section solution" aria-labelledby="solution-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">See one working approach</p>
          <h2 id="solution-title">Reference solution</h2>
          <details data-reveal="http-reference">
            <summary><span>Open the reference solution</span><span class="summary-label">Optional</span></summary>
            <div class="solution-copy">
              <p>
                The reference solution puts the rules on the product body and turns on
                ASP.NET Core's built-in validation for both writes. Quantity is from 1 to
                100. Name has a rule that rejects a value with no non-whitespace character.
                Validation runs before the handler. A failure is the 400 problem response,
                and the handler does not save. A valid body keeps the starter's 201, 204,
                and 404. The other valid approach is the same two checks inside the create
                handler and the replace handler, returning a validation problem and
                skipping the save. The trade-off is that each write has its own copy of
                the rules, so the copies can diverge. The plausible miss is treating name
                as a required string: the empty name is rejected, and the whitespace name
                is stored with 201.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="side-column" aria-label="Challenge setup">
        <section class="run-card" aria-labelledby="run-title">
          <p class="section-kicker">Your local proof</p>
          <h2 id="run-title">Clone, then test</h2>
          <p>
            Challenge directory: <code>request-validation</code>
          </p>
          <p>Setup: git and the .NET SDK.</p>
          <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/mustafaAshfaq/dotnet-challenges.git
cd dotnet-challenges/request-validation
dotnet test</code></pre>
          <a
            class="repo-link"
            href="https://github.com/mustafaAshfaq/dotnet-challenges/tree/main/request-validation"
          >
            Browse the challenge directory
          </a>
        </section>
        <section class="prerequisite" aria-labelledby="prerequisite-title">
          <p class="section-kicker" id="prerequisite-title">Prerequisite</p>
          <p>No prerequisite.</p>
        </section>
        <p class="completion-note">
          This catalog shows the requirements. The code and the proof run on your machine.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .challenge {
    padding-block: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .crumbs {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    margin-block-end: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .crumbs a {
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(17rem, 22rem);
    align-items: end;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-block: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem) 0.5rem;
  }

  .hero .eyebrow {
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .hero .eyebrow span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin-block-end: 0.9rem;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .hero-summary {
    max-width: 36ch;
    margin-block-end: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .content-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 22rem);
    align-items: start;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    padding-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .hero,
  .content-grid,
  .main-column,
  .side-column,
  .run-card {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .content-section + .content-section {
    margin-block-start: clamp(2.8rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .section-kicker {
    margin-block-end: 0.7rem;
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    margin-block-end: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .decision h2 {
    max-width: 62ch;
    padding-inline-start: 1rem;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--fail);
    font-family: var(--body);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-block-end: 1.2rem;
  }

  .effect-count {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .effect-contract,
  .effect-boundary {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-block: 1rem 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .effect-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .effect-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.9rem;
    padding-block: 1.2rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .effect-number {
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--pass);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .effect-list p {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  code,
  pre {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  p code,
  h2 code,
  li code {
    padding: 0.08rem 0.28rem;
    background: var(--mark);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .side-column {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .run-card {
    padding: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--pass);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .run-card h2 {
    margin-block-end: 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .run-card > p:not(.section-kicker) {
    margin-block-end: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .run-card pre {
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #f4f7f5;
    line-height: 1.7;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .repo-link {
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .prerequisite {
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--mark);
  }

  .prerequisite .section-kicker {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .prerequisite p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .completion-note {
    margin-block: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .disclosures {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.15rem;
  }

  details {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  summary {
    min-height: 3.25rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 700;
    list-style: none;
    transition: background-color 180ms ease-out;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  summary::after {
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    flex: none;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--pass);
    content: "+";
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  details[open] > summary::after {
    content: "−";
  }

  summary:hover {
    background: var(--canvas);
  }

  summary:active {
    background: var(--mark);
  }

  .summary-label {
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: right;
  }

  details > p,
  .solution-copy {
    padding: 0 0.95rem 1rem;
    margin-block-end: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .solution-copy p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  .solution > h2 {
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .solution details {
    border-color: var(--line);
    background: var(--mark);
  }

  .solution details > summary {
    min-height: 3.5rem;
  }

  .solution-copy {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }

  @media (min-width: 961px) {
    .side-column {
      position: sticky;
      top: 1.25rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero,
    .content-grid,
    .side-column {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .status-slip {
      order: -1;
      max-width: 28rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .challenge {
      padding-block-start: 0.75rem;
    }

    .crumbs {
      font-size: 0.8rem;
    }

    .status-slip {
      max-width: none;
    }

    .effect-list li {
      grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.65rem;
    }

    .effect-number {
      width: 1.75rem;
      height: 1.75rem;
    }

    .summary-label {
      font-size: 0.72rem;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    summary {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
